NOTE ON LICENSE CHOICE (remove this note before publishing if you like):
GPL-2.0-or-later is recommended because the repository builds and ships a modified
NetSurf (GPL-2.0), so the NetSurf patches in build.sh must be GPL-2.0 anyway, and a
single repo license avoids ambiguity. If you would rather keep only YOUR Lua code
under a permissive license (e.g. MIT) and treat the binaries as mere aggregation,
you may — but the NetSurf modifications in build.sh stay GPL-2.0 regardless.
